e color scheme to meet the specifications. Need to define specific colors for candle body outline and fill based on rising or falling trends. The default dark fill for a falling candle will be the background color.\n\nConsidering implementing a class-level or constant color palette for flexibility. This would allow for easier customization of the monochrome color scheme and maintain a clean code structure. The suggested palette includes up and down candle colors for body, outline and wick.\n\n\nExamining the existing candle drawing logic to handle Doji candles, where the body is very thin. A condition `height < 0.5` triggers drawing a horizontal line. The line for Doji should have a width of `body_width * 2`, placed at price `o`.\n\nAnalyzing the `generate_picture` function to locate the parameters defining candle characteristics. Observed the existing definitions for wick and body drawing, confirming the drawing order (wick first, then body) is crucial for correct Doji candle rendering. The next step is to integrate the Doji line drawing logic into the established structure, using the existing data and drawing primitives.\n\n\nThe code sets cosmetic pens ensuring consistent 1-pixel line widths regardless of zoom. Rising candles use a light gray fill, dark gray wicks and outline. Falling candles utilize a background-color fill, dark gray wicks, and a dark gray outline. Doji candles with very small bodies draw a horizontal line with the specified width.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"@'\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\ncandlestick_item.py — Графический элемент японских свечей для pyqtgraph.\\nМонохромная палитра в строгом стиле STRG / QUIK:\\n- Растущие (Up) свечи: светлое тело (#c0c0c0), контур (#cccccc)\\n- Падающие (Down) свечи: темное полое тело в цвет фона (#111111), контур (#555555)\\n- Косметические фитили 1px (setCosmetic) для четкости при любом зуме\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport pyqtgraph as pg\\nfrom PyQt6 import QtCore, QtGui\\n\\n\\nclas